Q: 415 HTTP response status when hitting an API response for a Java project with explicitly included JAR files A: <p>In mvnrepository.com, I see the groupId and artifactId different (see <a href="https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/javax.mail/javax.mail-api/1.6.2" rel="nofollow noreferrer">the JavaMail API JAR</a>)</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;!-- Source: https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/javax.mail/javax.mail-api --&gt;
&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;javax.mail&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;javax.mail-api&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;1.6.2&lt;/version&gt;
    &lt;scope&gt;compile&lt;/scope&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>If you're using 1.6.2 the <code>sun.com</code> packages are not used.</p>

Q: Angular Signal Forms: ERROR RuntimeError: NG01904: Orphan field, can&#39;t find element in array &lt;root&gt; A: <p>If you only need your model to have a country and a region, your interface should be like</p>
<pre><code>type CountryFormModel = {
  country: string | null;
  region: string | null;
};
</code></pre>
<p>//You declare, e.g.</p>
<pre><code>countryFormModel = signal&lt;CountryFormModel&gt;({
    country: 'Niederlande',
    region: 'Utrecht',
  });
//and
countryForm = form(this.countryFormModel);

</code></pre>
<p>You can use computed to change &quot;regions&quot; and also to check if region is included in the regions:</p>
<pre><code>  regions = computed(() =&gt; {
    const country=untracked(this.countryForm.country)?.value()
    const regions=this.countries.find(x=&gt;x.name==country)?.regions ?? []
    const region=untracked(this.countryFormModel).region
    if (!regions.find(x=&gt;x.name==region))
      untracked(this.countryFormModel).region=null

    console.log('computed')
    return regions
  });
</code></pre>
<p>See how you use <code>untracked</code> to avoid executed when the form or formModel change, only is executed if this.countryFrom.country.value() change</p>
<p>In .html you use</p>
<pre><code>&lt;mat-form-field&gt;
    &lt;mat-label&gt;country&lt;/mat-label&gt;
    &lt;mat-select [formField]=&quot;countryForm.country&quot;&gt;
        @for(country of countries; track country.name)
        {
            &lt;mat-option [value]=&quot;country.name&quot;&gt;{{ country.name }}&lt;/mat-option&gt;
        }
    &lt;/mat-select&gt;
&lt;/mat-form-field&gt;
&lt;mat-form-field&gt;
    &lt;mat-label&gt;region&lt;/mat-label&gt;
    &lt;mat-select [formField]=&quot;countryForm.region&quot;&gt;
        @for(region of regions(); track region.name)
        {
            &lt;mat-option [value]=&quot;region.name&quot;&gt;{{ region.name }}&lt;/mat-option&gt;
        }
    &lt;/mat-select&gt;
&lt;/mat-form-field&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>See that the <code>value</code> of the options are not the whole &quot;country&quot; or the whole &quot;region&quot; (only the &quot;name&quot;)</p>
